o 3D reshape/broadcast), pre-transposed weight load (no tl.trans), 3-arg tl.dot(hs,w,acc), tl.argmax selection, int64 store, python-list companion capture\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"two score arrays; bias selection-only; fp32 epilogue; top-2 sum per group; 4 groups; -inf sentinel; top-8 experts; bias-free companion via masked sum; +1e-20 then *scaling; int64/fp32 outputs; tail m_mask; all epilogue 2D\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"0fc8f5f9-1900-55f4-b7d8-acefecbead69\", \"num_tokens\": 6144, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"d6d0eb83-de2e-5a6d-ba23-ee72ae216708\", \"num_tokens\": 2048, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}, {\"uuid\": \"1d554a6c-1d9d-54c7-9ed9-6d4b50c95906\", \"num_tokens\": 2112, \"status\": \"RUNTIME_ERROR\", \"correct\": false, \"speedup\": null}], \"all_correct\": false, \"geomean_speedup\": null, \"decision\": \"discard\", \"decision_reason\": \"0/5 RUNTIME_ERROR again, identical to c001 despite a structurally very different (fully-2D) epilogue. This RULES OUT the 3D reshape/broadcast and tl.trans as the fault: the failing construct is COMMON to c001 and c002. Remaining shared suspects, none observable via traceback (evaluator exposes only RUNTIME_ERROR): (a) 3-arg tl.dot(hs,w,acc) [older Triton reads arg3 as trans_a -> type error], (b) tl.argmax(axis=1), (c) int64 tl.store from kernel, (d) tl.sigmoid on a [BLOCK_M,256] tile. Next candidate c003 removes (a),(b),(c) at once (manual acc+=tl.dot; max+min-index argmax replacement; kernel stores int32, torch casts to int64) since a blind RUNTIME_ERROR cannot be bisected one-const