candidate_plan\": \"c011 (parent c010): revert gate GEMM to bf16 HMMA (remove the fp32 tile upcast and input_precision='ieee'; acc += tl.dot(a_bf16, b_bf16)), keeping c010's exact routing + torch.topk output order. Single-variable perf change; precision proven comparison-irrelevant (c007==c009). Then tile/tune GEMM (BLOCK_M/BLOCK_K/num_stages>=2/num_warps) and consider re-fusing the two kernels to cut the logits DRAM round-trip + second launch.\"}\n{\"candidate\": \"c011\", \"parent\": \"c010\", \"source_sha256\": \"83de403196ce75a5341fec02162b925ccf41682bb927744bce784d3ffeb1c771\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T01:06:00Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"Matmul precision is comparison-irrelevant (c007==c009 byte-identical), so reverting the gate GEMM from input_precision='ieee' (true fp32, off the tensor-core path, ~3-4x slower on A800) to native bf16 HMMA (bf16 operands, fp32 accumulate) keeps 5/5 correctness while using fast tensor cores, giving a large speedup over c010's 0.8592x.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"bf16 HMMA fp32-accum\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1}, \"output_order\": \"torch.topk(sorted=False): first 7 by asc index, min-score expert last\", \"sigmoid\": \"1/(1+exp(-x))\", \"sentinel\": \"-1e30\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"byte-identical to c010 except GEMM operands stay bf16 (drop .to(fp32) upcast and input_precision='ieee'); routing epilogue + torch.topk order unchanged; precision proven comparison-irrelevant\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 1.82329648134368, \"max_abs\": 4.589557647705078e-06, \"max_rel\": 5.927932306803996e-06}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": t