ble-buffered, wider K, more warps). Note B-tile [64,256] bf16 x2 stages ~72KB > 48KB static cap, so this also tests Triton's dynamic-shared-memory opt-in on this A800 stack (expected to work; the c001-c006 RUNTIME_ERRORs were the python-list bug, proven by c007, NOT shared memory). If c012 faster+correct -> continue tiling (BLOCK_M=64, num_stages=3). If c012 RUNTIME_ERRORs -> opt-in is the limiter; fall back to a <=48KB config (BLOCK_M=64, BLOCK_K=32, num_stages=2). Later: re-fuse the two kernels to drop the logits[T,256] DRAM round-trip + second launch.\"}\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":9,"oldLines":3,"newStart":9,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"candidate\": \"c009\", \"parent\": \"c007\", \"source_sha256\": \"02657b0ad88d17f9add49ade3d5aef557b60e3c51e7c855b9845e22d018540f9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T00:28:10Z\", \"hypothesis\": \"The wrong selected SET in c007/c008 came from the bf16 gate GEMM diverging from the reference's fp32 F.linear; an exact fp32 GEMM (upcast bf16 tiles to fp32, tl.dot(input_precision='ieee') true-fp32 accumulate) with c007's descending-by-score emit will match the reference set+order and pass.\", \"config\": {\"arch\": \"two-kernel split\", \"gemm\": {\"BLOCK_M\": 16, \"BLOCK_K\": 32, \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1, \"precision\": \"ieee (fp32 upcast tiles, true fp32 accumulate)\"}, \"route\": {\"grid\": \"(T,)\", \"num_warps\": 4, \"num_stages\": 1}, \"output_order\": \"descending by masked (sigmoid+bias) score\", \"sigmoid\": \"1/(1+exp(-x))\", \"sentinel\": \"-1e30\"}, \"validation\": {\"static_gate_passed\": true, \"static_gate_notes\": \"identical to c007 except GEMM upcasts tiles to fp32 and uses input_precision='ieee'; with exact fp32 logits my group top-2 sum, top-4 groups, mask, and top-8 experts are provably the SAME SET as the reference (all fp32 deterministic); descending emit\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"INCORRECT_NUMERICAL\", \"correct\":