lots 0..6 by ascending expert index\"}, \"per_workload\": [{\"uuid\": \"469b2796-deb3-5a83-a7a6-1b2f84b86f20\", \"num_tokens\": 2240, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8858762985769966, \"max_abs\": 4.76837158203125e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.266351644830138e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"993dd417-9fb2-5d66-9b81-c1e15a113463\", \"num_tokens\": 2272, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8354636802460559, \"max_abs\": 4.917383193969727e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.565205351056647e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"0fc8f5f9-1900-55f4-b7d8-acefecbead69\", \"num_tokens\": 6144, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.9352054300402902, \"max_abs\": 5.364418029785156e-07, \"max_rel\": 8.381903171539307e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"d6d0eb83-de2e-5a6d-ba23-ee72ae216708\", \"num_tokens\": 2048, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8020239111201585, \"max_abs\": 4.917383193969727e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.805369932611939e-07}, {\"uuid\": \"1d554a6c-1d9d-54c7-9ed9-6d4b50c95906\", \"num_tokens\": 2112, \"status\": \"PASSED\", \"correct\": true, \"speedup\": 0.8434427620220671, \"max_abs\": 4.470348358154297e-07, \"max_rel\": 7.982765168890182e-07}], \"all_correct\": true, \"geomean_speedup\": 0.8591917965392462, \"arithmetic_mean_speedup\": 0.8604024164011136, \"decision\": \"champion\", \"decision_reason\": \"FIRST CORRECT CANDIDATE: 5/5 PASSED, max_abs ~5e-7 (essentially exact). The output-order hypothesis is CONFIRMED: torch.topk(sorted=False) on CUDA returns the 7 strictly-larger experts by ascending expert index followed by the min-score (kth-value) expert last. Combined with the exact-fp32 set this reproduces the reference to ulp. Geomean speedup 0.8592x -- CORRECT but SLOWER than the multi-launch reference; must now optimize. Root perf cost: (a) GEMM uses input_precision='ieee' (true fp32 dot) which on A800 is ~3-4x slower than bf16 HMMA and does NOT use the fast tensor-core path; (b) c007==c009 proved matmul precision is IRRELEVANT to the compared